From 98079a424f8ca8bd2c44d63a616ae626750572b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shifangx <shifangx@nvidia.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 22:02:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(nemotron-vl): serve the MTP block as an EAGLE draft

The Nemotron-H VL checkpoints carry the same Multi-Token Prediction block their
text siblings do, but nothing could reach it: the draft-model architecture swap
had no entry for them, so --speculative-algorithm EAGLE could not resolve a
draft model at all.

Three changes, and only two of them were obvious.

configs/model_config.py
  NemotronH_Omni_Reasoning_V3 and NemotronH_Nano_VL_V2 swap to
  NemotronHVLForCausalLMMTP. A separate block from the text entry because the
  draft class differs, and no num_nextn_predict_layers override because on
  these configs it lives on the nested llm_config, where the checkpoint already
  sets it.

models/nemotron_h_mtp.py
  NemotronHVLForCausalLMMTP(NemotronHForCausalLMMTP). The draft is a pure
  language model -- EAGLE's draft forward consumes
  forward_batch.spec_info.hidden_states and never touches pixels -- so the whole
  difference is where the config and the weight names live: unwrap
  config.llm_config, and rewrite the checkpoint's language_model. prefix.

  The rewrite goes through remap_prefix, the mechanism the parent already
  applies, rather than wrapping the weight iterator. Order is load-bearing:
  replace_prefix applies every matching rule in turn rather than stopping at
  the first, so language_model.backbone has to be consumed before the bare
  language_model.. Vision keys need no rule -- the parent's is_mtp filter drops
  every name without mtp in it, which is exactly the set a language draft does
  not own.

models/nano_nemotron_vl.py
  get_embed_and_head() / set_embed_and_head(), delegating to the nested
  language model. This is the one that is easy to miss: EAGLE calls
  get_embed_and_head on the *target* while wiring the draft up
  (speculative/eagle_worker_v2.py:328), NemotronHForCausalLM defines it so the
  draft inherits it, but the VL target class defined neither -- so the
  speculative path raised AttributeError on the target several minutes into
  engine startup, after the swap had already succeeded.

  It also explains why the draft's own load_weights never loads an embedding:
  is_mtp drops backbone.embeddings.weight, and that is correct rather than a
  bug, because NemotronHMultiTokenPredictor asserts "embed_tokens not
  initialized - must be shared from target model". The embedding arrives over
  this path.

Verified offline against the real checkpoint index: language_model.mtp.* keys
remap to mtp.* and survive the is_mtp filter, backbone and vision keys are
dropped, the text model's own remap is unchanged, and the method-resolution
chain gives the target get_embed_and_head and the draft set_embed_and_head.

Not verified by running. A draft with wrong weights does not raise -- sglang's
loader drops names it does not recognise -- it simply never gets accepted, so
the number that settles this is the accept rate against a no-speculation run
over the same prompts, not the absence of a traceback.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
